The platform personality matches on the class, not on the name

Run 574's panel said N-: the root nub has no name at all.  That is the
whole of it.

The root nub takes its name from the device tree's root node, and the
kernel replaces that name with the first string of the node's compatible
property -- but only when the tree is published, and the tree is published
when the platform expert starts, and the platform expert starts when it is
matched.  A personality that matches on the name therefore asks for a name
that does not exist yet: the matching drops it with "the nub does not
match the personality", the platform expert never starts, the tree is
never published, and the name is never set.  The board waits for a driver
that is waiting for the board to have a name.

So the personality matches on the class alone.  The root nub is an
IOPlatformExpertDevice and it is the only one, and the personality asks for
that class, and the passive match has nothing left to refuse.

And the failure that is kept for the panel is ours now, not the donor's:
the other drops are Apple's personalities asking for Apple nubs -- the
NVRAM service among them -- and they are not what this board is waiting
for.

